east lies…"],["Officers Club","sight",37.7973,-122.4592,"50 Moraga Ave","Tue-Sun 10AM-6PM","","","","r","Part of it was built by the Spanish with adobe walls in the late 1700s, and was remodeled in the 1930s in the Spanish Colonial Revival-style adorned with rustic Spanish-tile gable roofs, heavy, rough timber lintels and beams, and…"],["El Polin Spring","sight",37.7929,-122.4554,"El Polin Loop","","","","","r","El Polin spring water bubbles from a rock wall at the head of this riparian valley. The spring provided a source of fresh water for the Spanish Presidio, and Spanish and Mexican families built their homes in this sheltered valley.…"],["Lovers' Lane","sight",37.7978,-122.4545,"","","","","","r","One of the oldest foot trails in the Presidio, Lovers' Lane is an easy, one-mile walk. U.S. soldiers used the trail to visit their lovers and family in San Francisco."],["Presidio Golf Course","sight",37.7906,-122.4599,"300 Finley Rd","Tee-off times 6:45AM-3:09PM","","","","r","Founded in 1895 by the private San Francisco Golf and Country Club, the original 9-hole Presidio Golf Course was one of the earliest courses on the West Coast. In 1910, the course was expanded to 18-holes. Today, the course is open to…"],["Steps at Broadway and Lyon","activity",37.7933,-122.4465,"Pacific Heights","","","","","r","If you climb these steps you can get a breathtaking view of the Palace of Fine Arts, the Marina, and the Bay. The Steps are known locally as the \"San Francisco Stair Master\"... and with good reason!"],["Pluto's Fresh Food for a Hungry Universe","restaurant",37.8,-122.441,"3258 Scott St","Mon–Fri 11AM–10PM, Sat–Sun 10:30AM–10PM","","","","r","Fun American restaurant that's part of a chain. It's mostly green salads and sandwiches here &mdash; custom made to your discerning specifications!"]]}